From a825f11dfa8b9067aa2e2bc898f1256b885f7091 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: djnice <djnice@freemail.hu>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 12:02:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 61/67] mp4: DTS through the packetizer

A DTS-HD MA + DTS:X track of an MP4 (mp4a, esds object type 0xa9) was
passed through as DTS: the INFO panel said "bitstream dts", the receiver
got the core. The mp4 demuxer gives its esds tracks as packetized, so no
DTS packetizer looked at the frames, the profile stayed PROFILE_DTS and
the decoder told the audio output "dtshd" = false. The object type does
not tell either: this one (and other muxers') mark DTS-HD MA as 0xa9.

The esds DTS tracks now go through the packetizer, as the Matroska ones
do: it finds the extension substream after the core and sets
PROFILE_DTS_HD, the audio output takes the DTS-HD (HBR) path. The dtse /
dtsh / dtsl sample entries keep their own profile.

Message-Id: <20261120-dvfel-mp4-dts-packetizer@djnice>
---
 modules/demux/mp4/essetup.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/modules/demux/mp4/essetup.c b/modules/demux/mp4/essetup.c
index cd176f372f..2fc56ce2a9 100644
--- a/modules/demux/mp4/essetup.c
+++ b/modules/demux/mp4/essetup.c
@@ -88,6 +88,13 @@ static void SetupESDS( demux_t *p_demux, mp4_track_t *p_track, const MP4_descrip
         return;
     }
 
+    /* DTS: its frames through the packetizer, which tells DTS-HD (MA, DTS:X)
+     * from a core by the frames themselves (an extension substream after the
+     * core) and sets the profile the audio output passes DTS-HD by. The object
+     * type does not tell it: DTS-HD MA tracks are muxed as 0xa9 (DTS) too */
+    if( p_track->fmt.i_cat == AUDIO_ES && p_track->fmt.i_codec == VLC_CODEC_DTS )
+        p_track->fmt.b_packetized = false;
+
     p_track->fmt.i_original_fourcc = 0; /* so we don't have MP4A as original fourcc */
     p_track->fmt.i_bitrate = p_decconfig->i_avg_bitrate;
 
